Z||000000||fierospeeder||10-24-1999||04:09 AM||||This is my moms 2.8L v6 celebrity, but i got a fiero, so anyway, i was trying to change the fuel filter but i got a small pin hole leak on it, not bad at all, its only moist and not leaking a lot.  The whole line from the back to the front of the car is rusted and i want to replace the line from the filter to the front of the car.  My question is i should use steel tubing and should it be a double flare.  I never done this before and i have to buy the tools, flaring tube bender and a cutter, i have cut tubing before but never done this.  Can anyone give me some tips about doing this.  I seen a small how to in hot rod someplace on doing nitrous tubing on the intake but having 500 magazines of different types its hard to find.  thanks<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||10-25-1999||03:56 PM||||Yes! It must be steel line.<P>As for the double flair..... I can't remember for sure but I think it is doubled.||||reg||1
Z||000002||David||10-25-1999||04:30 PM||||Steel tubing is double flaired to prevent the flare from developing a crack.  Copper tubing doesn't have this problem because it is softer.  Buy, borrow, or rent a double flare set.  Don't take chances with fuel lines or brake lines. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||10-25-1999||08:01 PM||||i saw aluminum tubing for fuel lines in the summit catalog so i was wondering about that.<BR>thanks you guys, and im going to visit sears on the weekend.||||reg||1
